  "notes": "M.A./Ph.D. in Mythological Studies. The Master of Arts degree is awarded after the first two years of study and successful completion of a comprehensive examination (MS 800, 0 units, in Y2 Spring). Students continuing toward the doctorate engage in a third year of coursework including research courses and development of a concept paper for the dissertation. The fourth and fifth years focus on dissertation writing and research (MS 900, 15 units; MS 970, 3.5 units). On-campus residential format: during coursework years, the program meets nine times a year on campus (Fall and Winter quarters: three three-day sessions Fri-Sun; Spring quarter: two three-day sessions Fri-Sun and one four-day session Thu-Sun).",
